1000043,AS101 - Part 1,KH0114,Pachacamac,,"""Museum für Völkerkunde, Berlin""","1. Because only single knots are found on this quipu, the Aschers interpreted the lower knot cluster as the units position and the higher as the tens position.  This interpretation has not been followed.
2. AS101 consists of 2 quipus tied together.  The 2 parts are listed as AS101 - Part 1 and AS101 - Part 2.  The twisted ends of the main cords of the 2 parts are tied together with a square knot.
3. This is one of several quipus acquired by the Museum in 1907 with provenance Pachacamac.  See AS97 for a complete listing.
Additional notes are found in Ascher and Ascher 1987:700, 702-704.",19.0,SouthCentral,,U,,46.5,21,21,0.0,0.0,0,,0,,,38.0,0.0,0.8571428571428571,0.14285714285714285,0.0,0.5714285714285714,2,0.0
