1000413,UR149,KH0389,Hacienda Ullujalla y Callengo,,Museo Regional de Ica,"1) Top cords are inserted through the pendant cord attachments, free end inserted through twisted end. The top pendant falls to the right or left of the pendant cord groups. This is indicated by R or L on the data sheet.

2) In some cases, top cords appear to function as totalizers of pendant values only (i.e., not + sub. values)

T1: Looped end of cord to the Right. Tail comes off center of group
T2: Looped end to right. Tail in center.
T3: Looped to right. Tail on left.
T4: Looped to right. Tail on left.
T5: Looped to right. Tail on left.
T6: Loop to right. Tail on right. 
T7: Loop to left. Tail in middle. 
T8: Loop to right. Tail in middle. 
T9: Loop to right. Tail on left. 
T10: Loop to right. Tail in center.
T11: Loop to right. Tail on left. 
T12: Loop on right, tail in middle. 
T13: Loop on right; tail on left. 
T14: Loop on right, tail in middle. 
T15: Loop on left, tail on left.
T16: Loop on right, tail in middle. 
T17: Loop on left, tail in middle. ",28.0,SouthCentral,P,,CN,35.5,266,192,0.0,0.0,263,0.0,264,0.0,1.0,16.5,0.0,0.5150375939849624,0.007518796992481203,0.462406015037594,0.44360902255639095,3,2.9270833333333335
