1000521,UR210,KH0448,Ica/Pisco,"""South Coast, Peru""","""Ethnologisches Museum, Berlin, Germany""","Observations:
1) Primary cord connected with decorative cord: twisted end of primary cord of UR 210 is opened near the beginning (1.0 cm.), one attachment cord (W) is passed through opening in ply of primary cord and through an opening in the twisted end of the decorative cord. The attachment cord is then knotted. Length of attachment cord after knotting is 42.0 cm. Attachment cord: W, S-ply, 0.08 cm thickness. 

2) Decorative cord: Length: 21.0 cm, AB-GG-(Ab-GG), 0.29 thickness. At 21.0 cm decorative cord enters needlework bundle (see drawing). Length of bundle: 3.0 cm. with additional 5.0 cm of red (RM) and white (W) tassel.

3) Pendants 8 and 9 are knotted together with additional cord, apparently identical to those on UR 211 in that two of the three additional cords carry tufted knots, see drawing.",23.0,SouthCentral,P,Z,CN,0.0,78,32,0.0,0.0,77,0.0,78,0.0,1.0,36.5,0.0,0.8974358974358975,0.0,0.0641025641025641,0.10256410256410256,2,2.65625
1000522,UR211,KH0449,Ica/Pisco,"""South Coast, Peru""","""Ethnologisches Museum, Berlin, Germany""","Missing sheet with primary cord information (note added 2013). Refer to sheets for values of knots. 

Observations:

1) Primary cord of UR 211 knotted with primary cord of UR 210. See drawing. 

2) Sling attached to primary cord fo UR 211: looped end of braided sling around primary cord. Loop of 3.0 cm. on each side of primary cord, loop is made from red (RM) camelid fibers wrapped around vegetal fiber (AB) cord fo sling. Length of sling: 98.0 cm including beginning loop and terminal braid. Terminal braid: 4-corner braid composed of vegetal fibers (AB) and red (RM) camelid fibers. Terminal braid lenght: 4.0 cm. Thickness: 0.56 cm. Drawing attached. 

3) Tufted knots: Tufted knots are composed of thin plied threads passed through one ply of a plied pendant cord, then doubled and knotted. The excess thread beyond the knot has been cut, leaving a 'tufted' appearance to the end of the knot. 
Sample tufted knot doubled thread thicknesses: 0.13 cm, 0.10 cm, 0.11 cm
End of tuft: 0.44 cm, 0.74 cm, 0.67 cm, 0.58 cm",23.0,SouthCentral,P,,CN,74.0,95,83,0.0,0.0,95,0.0,95,0.0,1.0,47.0,0.0,0.7473684210526316,0.0,0.25263157894736843,0.0,1,0.012048192771084338
