1000562,HP033,KH0565,"Ullujaya, Ocucaje, Ica",,"Museo Nacional de Arqueología, Antropología e Historia del Perú","1. The khipu is sewn to a cotton cloth, light brown, 66.0 cm x 50.0 cm. Adhered is a ticket that says ""Uyujaya/1964."" The position of the khipu on the cloth is backwards so that the final part is at the beginning end. However, the description of the cords is done accurately.
2. Pendant 17 has a simple knot, direction Z, that is bigger than the typical knots; at 1.0 cm. from the final knot, that seems to be a marker.
3. The primary cord has the same characteristics as pendants 5 to 8, 13 to 16 and 21 to 24. 
4. subsidiary 2.3, the red thread is camelid wool dyed red.",,,P,,CN,31.0,28,27,0.0,0.0,28,0.0,28,0.0,1.0,25.5,0.0,0.8214285714285714,0.07142857142857142,0.10714285714285714,0.14285714285714285,2,3.037037037037037
1000563,HP034,KH0566,"Ullujaya, Ocucaje, Ica",,"Museo Nacional de Arqueología, Antropología e Historia del Perú","1. The khipu is attached to a frame.
