3. There is evidence that between cords 51 and 55 there existed 3 other pendants; however, upon assembling the khipu with thread between said cords, seven pendants that presumably pertained to the khipu were detached. It is impossible to determine which of these cords were 52, 53, and 54, and the information for these seven pendants has been omitted from the description of the khipu. The information is presented at the end. In the statistics tables, corresponding information is included. 
4. Attachment of segments 1 and 2 at 6.0 cm. ",,,P,,CN,44.0,82,56,0.0,0.0,82,0.0,82,0.0,1.0,42.5,0.0,0.9512195121951219,0.012195121951219513,0.036585365853658534,0.0,1,3.4642857142857144
