1000574,HP045,KH0574,"Región Sur, Quillagua, Valle de Loa",,"Museo Nacional de Arqueología, Antropología e Historia del Perú","1. The principal cord has three wrapped cords. The first and third are light brown and white; there are only scarce remnants of the second cord.
