1000604,UR263,KH0499,Incahuasi,,Proyecto Incahuasi,"Second Kallanka, sector A, Subsector 1, UA 2, Unit 2K, UE 8
Observations; 
1) Although fragmentary, this khipu was excavated by G Urton at Incahuasi. The fragments were wrapped together. Therefore, the presumption is that this was a single, united khipu. 
2) Excavation: January 11, 2014 (see photos) 
3) There are three fragments. 
4) UR263 was wrapped together with a smaller khipu, recorded as UR262
5) Fragment #1 is V attached; however, fragments #2 and #3 are R attached. Thus, the sequence of cords recorded in fragment #1 (which ends at cord 108) should be reversed, to coincide with cord order in fragments #2 and #3
6) Nickname: Khipu Urton
7) Fragments: 59.5 cm + 13 cm + 50 cm. ",,,P,S,CN,122.5,237,122,0.0,0.00819672131147541,237,0.0,237,0.0,1.0,28.0,0.0,0.48945147679324896,0.0,0.510548523206751,0.004219409282700422,2,2.8852459016393444
