1000610,UR268,KH0505,Incahuasi,,Proyecto Incahuasi ,"Sector A, Subsector 1, CA - UA 4, Unidad 20N, UE 18
Nickname: Khipu Mani
Needlework bundle and red tassel at beginning
Observations: 
1) Cord 60S1 is attached at top as a subsidiary but the end is inserted through the ply of cord 60 (see drawing)
2) Cord 96 has sub. 96S1 at 5.5 c.m. Cord 96 is then inserted into ply of 96S1 at 31 c.m. and ends
3) As for the structure of numerical values in UR268, one of the ""khipu del Mani"", if we look from the beginning to the end of the khipu, one could say that from #1 - #92, the basic structure is as follows: 
1 - Big # (in thousands
2 - 208
3 - around 1,000 + 1
3S1 - Number in 10s
4 - another big #, in thousands
However, from around cord #93, the structure is generally as follows: 
1 - big #
2 - 208
3 - result of big # - 208
Does this shift in numerical organization and structure represent some basic, operational change, or evolution? E.g., perhaps it is a move from a complex dispersal of values among several parties to one between three entities: 
1 - income/input entity
2 - fixed sum (from governing entity)
3 - operational sum/entity
",,,P,S,CN,131.0,169,135,0.014814814814814815,0.2,169,0.0,169,0.0,1.0,40.5,0.0,0.591715976331361,0.0,0.40828402366863903,0.22485207100591717,4,4.355555555555555
